# FestPilot Project Brain

FestPilot is a festival companion app. It helps festival-goers (1) pick every artist they want to see, (2) turn those favorites into a conflict-free personal timetable, and (3) stay together with friends through a shared group timetable, a stage map, walking-time awareness, live presence, and temporary meeting points. Julio is the Product Lead and developer.

## Before answering about FestPilot, read the relevant files in FestPilot/brain/:

- `FestPilot/brain/README.md` — Entry point with truth policy and file index
- `FestPilot/brain/product-spec.md` — What the app is, features, rules, scope (the first source of truth)
- `FestPilot/brain/decision-log.md` — All decisions with status (DEC-NNN)
- `FestPilot/brain/technical-direction.md` — Stack, data source, architecture, infra
- `FestPilot/brain/project-status.md` — Current status, pending tasks, next steps
- `FestPilot/brain/research/` — Research outputs and raw source material (e.g. the festival data-source study)

## Critical rules — NEVER contradict these:

- Brain files are the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for product decisions
- If a decision is not in decision-log.md, it has NOT been made
- The AI must READ brain files before answering product questions
- Code output must always be in English (variable names, comments, etc.)
- Documents follow the language of the request
- Lineup data is never hardcoded: resolve the source (event + uuid) from the official page, then fetch the CDN JSON (see technical-direction.md)

